## File Operations

### Available Operations

- `list`: List files in a folder or root
- `read`: Get file metadata and download URL
- `upload`: Upload a new file
- `delete`: Delete a file
- `move`: Move file to different folder

### File Structure

```json
{
  "id": "file_abc123",
  "name": "report.pdf",
  "type": "application/pdf",
  "size": 102400,
  "url": "https://storage.emery.ai/...",
  "folder_id": "folder_xyz",
  "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z"
}
```

### Listing Files

```
# List all files in root
file_crud(method="list")

# List files in specific folder
file_crud(method="list", folder_id="folder_xyz")
```

### Uploading Files

When uploading, provide:
- `name`: Filename with extension
- `content`: Base64 encoded content OR
- `url`: URL to fetch file from
- `folder_id`: (optional) Target folder

```
file_crud(method="upload",
          name="document.pdf",
          content="base64_encoded_content...",
          folder_id="folder_xyz")
```

### Reading Files

Get file metadata and download URL:
```
file_crud(method="read", file_id="file_abc123")
```

The response includes a temporary download URL.

### Important Notes

- File IDs are UUID strings (not numeric)
- Folder IDs are also UUID strings
- Maximum file size depends on org plan
- Supported types: PDF, images, documents, spreadsheets
- URLs are temporary and expire after a period
